From 0a8db5b43f94da1d98b34dc95dbc6e749e5d1a79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: u1131128 <hipac1@lsalab.cs.nthu.edu.tw>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:11:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] Let the RHS fluxes be the Riemann solver's output buffers
 on the inviscid path

s_finalize_riemann_solver copied flux_rsx_vf into flux_n and flux_src_rsx_vf(adv%beg) into flux_src_n element
for element, every sweep: both are (x, y, z) ordered in every direction. When the only readers are the flux
differences and CBC, which stay inside (-1:m, -1:n, -1:p), allocate the solver buffers in m_rhs and point
flux_n(1)%vf(l)%sf and flux_src_n(1)%vf(adv%beg)%sf at them (bounds remapped to -1), before anything is
attached on the device; finalize then skips those copies. Viscous, surface tension, chemistry, hypoelastic,
QBMM, bubbles, IBM, relativity, cylindrical, alpha-interface and dual-pass runs keep their own arrays.
Bit-identical (same values, no copy). Frees sys_size+1 halo-sized fields.
---
 src/simulation/m_rhs.fpp             |  43 ++++++++--
 src/simulation/m_riemann_solvers.fpp |   6 +-
 src/simulation/m_riemann_state.fpp   | 119 ++++++++++++++++-----------
 3 files changed, 112 insertions(+), 56 deletions(-)

